Maura,

it seems that you did not install rJava with JRI support. Please read  
the installation output carefully! Make sure you have configured Java  
in R *before* installing rJava - i.e. issue install.packages("rJava")  
and make sure JRI is enabled. If it's not, then you either don't have  
R shared library or you are missing a JDK. (BTW: please post full  
output only, it seems that you have removed the most important  
information from the output below)

Cheers,
Simon


