Message-ID: <D9A7281B-EA82-4F25-B215-75A1BC4B7101@r-project.org>

Maura,

rJava and JavaGD are packages that JGR depends on. Since you installed  
them *before* having a correct configuration, they don't contain  
everything that JGR needs. After fixing your R, you re-installed JGR  
only and thus both packages are still out of date. Simply run
install.packages("rJava")
and
install.packages("JavaGD")
as root in R in order to re-install them.

On Feb 9, 2008, at 5:16 PM, Maura E Monville wrote:

> The installation guidelines are not clear to me as they jump from  
> one platform to another one.
> There is no clearly stated installation ordered steps.
>

Actually there is:
http://www.rosuda.org/JGR/linux.shtml

If you followed them you'd save yourself the trouble ;). Linux  
distributions are a big mess, so you're pretty much on you own if you  
don't follow them by the letter - that's Linux :P

Cheers,
Simon



